s a very low card.\n\nReason: As the "Downstream" peasant (acting just before the Landlord), my role is to attack and force the Landlord to play high cards. Beating my teammate\'s 5 with an 8 is the optimal play because:\n1. It prevents the Landlord (who plays next) from sliding under with a low card like a 6 or 7.\n2. The ♦8 is an isolated single in my hand (since I want to keep 66 as a pair and 777 as a triplet), making it "trash" that I need to clear.\n3. It forces the Landlord to use a higher card (like a King or Ace) to win the trick, which I can then crush with my 2s or Joker to take the lead.\nPassing here would be too passive given my hand strength.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦8"]}'}
