g, but it consumes my only single Ace. It interferes with my teammate\'s potential plan and leaves me vulnerable if the Landlord has the Red Joker or 2s to control the game later.\n3.  **Play ♣2**: I possess a strong triplet of 2s (♠2, ♥2, ♣2). Breaking this triplet to play a single 2 significantly weakens my hand structure and endgame potential.\n4.  **Play Black Joker**: This is an overkill move that wastes my highest card on a non-critical turn.\n\nReason: My teammate has taken the initiative with a strong card (King). As a Peasant, I should not fight my teammate unless necessary. Passing forces the Landlord to spend high cards or yield control to my teammate. I should preserve my strong hand (Triplet 2s, Black Joker) to control the Landlord later in the game.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
